 THIS FILE WAS WRITTEN IN THE FORMAT OF THE 14-7-21  VERSION
      w                                   
          34 number of node parameters
           5 number of global variables

          27 functions

           0 L1 if 0 treat each spherical node as a cell and each cylinder as a cell
           0 L2 0 no screening, 1 screening by Gabriel method
           0 L3 0 there is torsion: scalar product between within cell ellipses, 1 there is no torsion
           0 L4 if 1 this forces apoptosis of all the nodes or cells that lose contact with others
           0 L5 1, for Euler numerical int., 0 for Runge-Kutta order 4 for movement, 2 R-K also for genetics
           0 L6 epithelial node plastic deformation (0=ON)
           0 L7 dynamic delta (0) / fixed delta (1)
           0 L8 neighboring algorithm: exhaustive by %add sphere (0) / by 3D triangulation (1)
           0 L9 1 for original 2016 version, 0 for 2021 version
           0 L10 if 0 volume conservation in cylinders
           0 L11 diffusion of reqcr (1=ON)
           0 L12 1 for adaptive size step (it uses Runge-Kutta), 2 to make for genetics too
           0 L13 this allows growth to add more than one node per cell per iteration
           0 L14 return the control in real time(0) or in real iterations(1), only with dynamic delta
           0 L15 random noise mode: 1 = biased random noise by energies , 0 = unbiased random noise
           0 L16 forces by diff. equations: 0 = activated, 1 = disabled (should go by energies)
           0 L17 if 0 epithelial nodes from one side do not consider as neighbors nodes from the other side
           0 L18 if 0 makes that single node cells divide gradually by adding a small daughter cell
           0 L19 if 0 cell polarization and directed division activated by the same wa (only for single node)
           0 L20 if 0 There is a limit in the attraction forces suffered by the nodes
           0 L21 if 1 we apply filters
           0 L22 if 1 silent mode: we do not print info each iteration
           0 L23 The neighs are only the nodes in the ADD range (0) we use an extended range (1)
           0 L24 if 0 we run the algorithm that recovers lost neighbors (assumes ffu(23)=0)
           0 L25 Nutrients limited. If 0 there is a limit to sum of cell cycle increase in each iteration
           0 L26 if 0 genetic changes in node properties happen gradually
           0 L27 if 0 we call to neighbor_build only once per iteration (assumes Rungekutta)

          13 filters: active, lethal, how often is checked

           0           0           0 WHICHEND 1: Over 4h of computation time
           0           0           0 WHICHEND 2: A node has too many neighbors
           0           0           0 WHICHEND 3: The total size is too big
           0           0           0 WHICHEND 4: There are too many nodes
           0           0           0 WHICHEND 5: No nodes
           0           0           0 WHICHEND 6: No movement
           0           0           0 WHICHEND 7: Time ended (iterations)
           0           0           0 WHICHEND 8: Time ended (real time)
           0           0           0 WHICHEND 9: The maximum ADD value is larger than 3 times the minimum ADD value
           0           0           0 WHICHEND 10: The average number of boxes per box is higher than maxnbox (parameter)
           0           0           0 WHICHEND 11: No movement
           0           0           0 WHICHEND 12: Broken epithelium
           0           0           0 WHICHEND 13: Blackholes (many nodes in the same place)

